                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "39f58b73-d5ca-3345-a395-14ead501bd96",
                        "entry_id": "c0ba179a-c615-311c-8bfd-4da8aa7beeb8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To be suspended or expelled temporarily from the university, either compulsorily or voluntarily."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "ambitransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "84f019ba-5385-45bf-8da5-fc374a0349e9",
                                "sense_id": "39f58b73-d5ca-3345-a395-14ead501bd96",
                                "text": "I was very unwell, so I had to rusticate for a year."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5833eff2-6570-4ba7-bbb2-6ae977f5b165",
                                "sense_id": "39f58b73-d5ca-3345-a395-14ead501bd96",
                                "text": "The college rusticated him after he failed all his exams."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "506a143b-4aed-41b4-b6d9-be94e1c69871",
                                "sense_id": "39f58b73-d5ca-3345-a395-14ead501bd96",
                                "text": "Pen looked at his early acquaintance,—who had been plucked, who had been rusticated, who had only, after repeated failures, learned to read and write correctly, and who, in spite of all these drawbacks, had attained the honour of a degree."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8aa1cb8c-7f12-4bbd-ac5b-9975e7de47a6",
                                "sense_id": "39f58b73-d5ca-3345-a395-14ead501bd96",
                                "text": "\"You don't think he'll rusticate us, or any thing of that sort?\" said Tom, who had felt horrible twinges at the captain's picture of the effects of rustication on ordinary mortals."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c322d537-c582-3560-ac25-2010dc9cc679",
                        "entry_id": "c0ba179a-c615-311c-8bfd-4da8aa7beeb8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To construct so as to produce jagged or heavily textured surfaces."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9c5e7c53-1315-382d-b30b-b411d989b8a8",
                        "entry_id": "c0ba179a-c615-311c-8bfd-4da8aa7beeb8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To compel to live in or to send to the countryside; to cause to become rustic."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8e504b50-416f-376c-96c7-afaeca13aa85",
                        "entry_id": "c0ba179a-c615-311c-8bfd-4da8aa7beeb8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To go to reside in the country."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "aa4f3fcc-1e76-4b29-8c3e-c21d695fc8bd",
                                "sense_id": "8e504b50-416f-376c-96c7-afaeca13aa85",
                                "text": "So alarming did the state of my finances become, that I soon realized that I must either leave the metropolis and rusticate somewhere in the country, or that I must make a complete alteration in my style of living."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9f432ca3-5a18-4c4e-b52d-4571808de6a9",
                        "source_entry_id": "c0ba179a-c615-311c-8bfd-4da8aa7beeb8",
                        "source_sense_description": "suspend or expel from a college or university",
                        "target_lang_word": "vyloučit ze studií",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f2cea9de-7966-472e-a648-3e83b3327535",
                        "source_entry_id": "c0ba179a-c615-311c-8bfd-4da8aa7beeb8",
                        "source_sense_description": "suspend or expel from a college or university",
                        "target_lang_word": "limoger",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "limoger",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4936decf-b641-338e-b3ff-e74840f1ab6a",
                                        "entry_id": "33a61e8c-95a2-3612-a382-0e9750df397c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Destituer un officier général de ses fonctions. Le terme « limoger » ne s'applique, par analogie, que pour des personnes occupant un poste élevé."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d72400e5-5b6f-4b96-91fa-135f941e7701",
                                                "sense_id": "4936decf-b641-338e-b3ff-e74840f1ab6a",
                                                "text": "Le gouvernement limogeait les chefs, et nommait le général Pétain — (Roger Martin du Gard, Épil., 1940, p.812)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96b4fac9-350f-40cf-af9c-6c281d93a02b",
                                                "sense_id": "4936decf-b641-338e-b3ff-e74840f1ab6a",
                                                "text": "Mme Verdurin disait : « C’est désolant, je vais téléphoner à Bontemps de faire le nécessaire pour demain, on a encore « caviardé » toute la fin de l’article de Norpois et simplement parce qu’il laissait entendre qu’on avait « limogé » Percin. » Car la bêtise courante faisait que chacun tirait sa gloire d’user des expressions courantes, et croyait montrer qu’elle était ainsi à la mode comme faisait une bourgeoise en disant, quand on parlait de M. de Bréauté ou de Charlus : « Qui ? Bebel de Bréauté, Mémé de Charlus ? »"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29e50668-5bd9-4ee5-a336-8b575ac3e718",
                                                "sense_id": "4936decf-b641-338e-b3ff-e74840f1ab6a",
                                                "text": "Selon lui, la fin de l’exigence remonte à l’épilogue de l’ère Hubert Fournier, limogé en décembre 2015 : « Durant les trois ans et demi avec Bruno Genesio, il y avait des excuses à tout va pour surprotéger et dédouaner les joueurs »."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "73eb46fb-1d9f-4cb4-b506-f4da84512905",
                        "source_entry_id": "c0ba179a-c615-311c-8bfd-4da8aa7beeb8",
